<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Holliday returns five weeks into treatment. The isolate is susceptible to isoniazid, rifampin, pyrazinamide, and ethambutol, and ethambutol was stopped a week ago when the result arrived. The three sputum smears collected in the third week were negative, and with his clinical improvement and more than two weeks of treatment he was released from home isolation two weeks ago and returned to work the following week. His cough is now occasional and dry, and the night sweats have stopped. He has taken every dose by video. He has no nausea now, no yellowing, dark urine, abdominal pain, numbness, or vision change. He has not had a drink in three weeks and has met his counselor twice. His roommate&apos;s first blood test was negative and will be repeated by the health department. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Susceptibility</td><td>Susceptible to all four first-line drugs; ethambutol stopped a week ago</td></tr><tr><td>Infection control</td><td>Three negative smears; released from isolation and back at work</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Occasional dry cough; no night sweats</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>None for three weeks; two counseling sessions</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

